Actually, let me look at the `match` function's FILE_USE handling. In the current HEAD version, the FILE_USE case is in `mget`. But the fix commit `2e9d1811` was in `mget` too (in a later version). Let me look at the current HEAD version of the FILE_USE case in mget.

In the current HEAD version:
```c
case FILE_USE:
        if (nbytes < offset)
                return 0;
        rbuf = m->value.s;
        if (*rbuf == '^') {
                rbuf++;
                flip = !flip;
        }
        if (file_magicfind(ms, rbuf, &ml) == -1) {
                file_error(ms, 0, "cannot find entry `%s'", rbuf);
                return -1;
        }
        (*name_count)++;
        oneed_separator = *need_separator;
        if (m->flag & NOSPACE)
                *need_separator = 0;
        rv = match(ms, ml.magic, ml.nmagic, s, nbytes, offset + o,
            mode, text, flip, indir_count, name_count,
            printed_something, need_separator, returnval);
        if (rv != 1)
            *need_separator = oneed_separator;
        return 1;
```

Here `rv` is assigned from `match(...)`. So `rv` is always initialized. This is not the bug.

